ome to this park to think and to pray quietly.","People from all over the world fold paper cranes and send them here as wishes for peace."));Lt("hiroshima_kids",Rt("We folded one thousand paper cranes for our school! My crane is the yellow one.",'折り鶴 — orizuru — means "folded crane". People say a thousand cranes grant a wish.'));Lt("hiroshima_cook",Rt("Okonomiyaki: cabbage first, then pork, then the crepe. Hiroshima-style is a tower, not a mix.","Flip it only once. Show off with the spatula — that is the tradition."));Lt("hiroshima_tram",Rt("The tram goes slowly, so you can see the city. And it never runs out of seats at this stop."));Lt("hiroshima_old",Rt("This city rebuilt itself with its heart in the right place. Be kind to each other, and eat well."));Lt("hiroshima_jogger",Rt("I run along the river each morning. It is calm, and the water is clean."));Lt("miyajima_guide",Rt("Welcome to Miyajima, the shrine island. Itsukushima Shrine has stood over the water for centuries.","At high tide the red torii seems to float. At low tide you can walk right up to it."));Lt("miyajima_seller",Rt("Hot oysters! Grilled with a squeeze of lemon.","And momiji manju — the island invented them."));Lt("miyajima_deer",Rt("A small deer sniffs at your bag. Hold on to your map and your snacks."));Lt("sign_miyajima",Rt("厳島神社 — Itsukushima Shrine. The great torii stands in the sea beyond this walkway."));Lt("fukuoka_staff",[_i("Welcome to Hakata.","ようこそ、博多へ。"),_i("Trains to Hiroshima, Osaka and Tokyo leave from this hall.")]);Lt("fukuoka_map",Rt("Area map: Hakata Station north, the shopping streets and ramen shops in the middle, the Nakasu river with food stalls, and Ōhori Park to the south."));Lt("fukuoka_tourist",Rt("Everyone told me to eat at the yatai stalls by the river. I came for the ramen but stayed for the gyoza.","The locals are so friendly!"));Lt("fukuoka_student",Rt('Hakata people speak in a gentle, rolling way. Instead of "da" we say "tai" or "bai".',`「そうたい！」 means "that's rig